course: dictionary
lesson: 10717
title: Unusually: different from normal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unusually means in a way that is not usual or normal. Look at the words around it for clues. «The sky was unusually dark at noon, so we switched on the lights.» Noon is normally bright, so unusually must mean not in the normal way.
explain: Unusually can also mean more than usually, or very. «The river was unusually cold» means it was colder than rivers normally are. To check, swap in your meaning: does «more than usually cold» still make sense? It does, so you have understood it.
explain: Scientists use this word when something breaks a usual pattern. «El Niño is a pattern every few years in which the eastern tropical Pacific becomes unusually warm, changing weather around the world.» The sea is warmer than its usual temperature, so scientists notice it and measure it.
fact: Unusually means in a way that is not usual or normal.
fact: Unusually also means more than usually, or very: «unusually cold» means colder than normal.
fact: Unusually often goes with words like large, early and quiet: «unusually large», «unusually early».
fact: In a story, «she was unusually quiet» is a clue that something may be wrong.
fact: El Niño is a pattern that happens every few years, when the eastern tropical Pacific becomes unusually warm.
exercise: «The shop was unusually busy for a Monday.» What does unusually suggest? | *More busy than normal | Empty and quiet | Closed for the day | Full of fish
exercise: In «She was unusually quiet at dinner», which word tells you the quietness was not normal for her? | *unusually | quiet | she | dinner
exercise: Why might a scientist write «unusually warm» about the sea? | It is colder than ice | It means the sea is always blue | *It is warmer than its usual temperature | It is a word for a fish
test: In «the eastern tropical Pacific becomes unusually warm», what does unusually mean? | Cold like ice | Calm and still | *Warmer than its usual temperature | Dark and deep
test: What is the best meaning of «unusually early»? | Very slowly | In a cave | *Earlier than normal | Late in the day
exam: Which sentence best shows unusually meaning not normal? | The snowman had a carrot nose. | We ate lunch at school. | *The snow fell in June, unusually for our town. | The snow was white and soft.
